  "body": "Running `web/build-app-wasm.sh` in a checkout leaves `Cargo.lock` modified: the `flecs_ecs` 0.2.2 and `flecs_ecs_sys` 0.2.1 entries lose their `source` and `checksum` lines, because the script builds with `cargo --config patch.crates-io...` pointing at its patched copies and cargo writes that resolution back into the workspace lock file.\n\nSeen 2026-11-12 during the v0.18.0 cut (the script was started by accident from a shell heredoc): the release branch's tree turned dirty and the stray change had to be restored with `git checkout -- Cargo.lock` before the release command could run.\n\nExpected: the script leaves the working tree as it found it - build against a copy of the lock file (e.g. `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` plus a temporary manifest dir, or save and restore `Cargo.lock` in a trap), and say so in its header.\n\nDone means: `git status --short` is empty after a successful and after a failed run of the script.\n",
